26.10.15
	ALIRT-0.6.0 multi-architecture release.
	- mod_hunter / process_hunter: real page-table walkers for armv7
	  (classic 2-level + LPAE), aarch64 (4K/16K pages, 3-5 levels,
	  folded-level aware), mips (o32), powerpc (ppc64 ELFv2, hash/radix
	  via init_mm) and riscv (sv39/sv48, 2GB low-window fallback for
	  4.19-5.12); arch header auto-selected from the target kernel's
	  CONFIG_*; build: make ARCH=<platform> [CROSS_COMPILE=] [KDIR=].
	- compat: ppc64 ELFv2 global-entry resolution of
	  kallsyms_lookup_name (KPROBES-based, exact prologue match).
	- mod_hunter: scan window anchored on THIS_MODULE on arm64
	  (KASLR-randomized module region); VMALLOC_START gate defused on
	  non-x86 architectures (addr_valid remains the authority).
	- CI: QEMU runtime detection matrix extended to 5 architectures
	  (aarch64, armv7, mips, powerpc, riscv) on kernels 6.12.35 /
	  6.18.56 / 7.2.10 — 28 matrix jobs, all green; per-arch QEMU
	  launch parameters and a pure-syscall static init (tests/init-cross.c)
	  replace the per-arch busybox rootfs.
	- Tests: hide_self sample now erases its list pointers Diamorphine-
	  style (real rootkit shape).

26.10.15
	ALIRT-0.5.2 LTS coverage release.
	- CI: added the longterm kernel 6.18 and the stable kernel 7.2 to
	  the build + QEMU runtime detection matrix (x86_64): 3.10, 4.4,
	  4.19, 5.4, 5.15, 6.12, 6.18, 7.2; aarch64 cross-builds for 5.15
	  and 6.12.
	- compat: forward-port SLUB / module layout adaptations to 6.18
	  and 7.2 kernel APIs (see commits).

26.10.14
	ALIRT-0.5.1 reliability release: fixes proven by the full CI matrix
	(compile + QEMU hidden-module detection green on 3.10 - 6.12 x86_64
	and 5.15/6.12 aarch64).
	- mod_hunter: fix module_kset double-dereference (report-time oops on
	  4.19/5.4/5.15, hang on 6.12); resolve init_mm/module_kset/'modules'
	  via kallsyms (none are exported; insmod previously failed);
	  RONX-era core_size heuristic dropped (0 scan candidates on <= 4.4);
	  layout-verified private kmem_cache_node copy for 3.10 - 6.1.
	- process_hunter / sock_hunter: complete private SLUB struct copies
	  where the kernel hides the definitions (include linux/slub_def.h
	  for kmem_cache/kmem_cache_cpu on 3.18 - 6.11).
	- modumper: replace vfs_write (unexported since 4.14) with the
	  file's f_op->write.
	- compat: fix kprobe pre_handler signature (pt_regs argument).

26.10.14
	ALIRT-0.5.0 the modernization release: renamed to ALIRT, moved to GitHub.
	- mod_hunter: merged nitara2 engine (thanks g1inko/ksen-lin, Phrack 71);
	  tri-source cross-validation (memory scan vs module list vs module kset)
	  to counter KoviD-class rootkits; seq_file /proc output (dmesg kept);
	  reveal downgraded to report-only on kernels >= 4.0.
	- process_hunter / sock_hunter: rewritten for the SLUB allocator
	  (2.6.32 - 6.12); sock_hunter adds IPv6 support.
	- modumper: modernized for core_layout / mem[] module layouts; on
	  kernels >= 5.10 dumps via /proc/get_mod + dump-extract.sh.
	- dismod: replaced the vendored 2005 binutils copy with dismod.sh
	  (system objdump, multi-arch).
	- CI: per-kernel-version build + QEMU runtime detection matrix
	  (3.10 - 6.12, x86_64/aarch64), compatibility table auto-published.
	- Docs: DKMS+MOK signing guide, trusted-media IR procedure
	  (Chinese, with PDF), README.zh-CN.

